---
title: Kedgeree
servings: 6
course: Main
locale: en
difficulty: Medium
cuisine: Scottish
---

Boil the @eggs{2} for ~{10%minutes}, then hold under cold running water.

Put the @undyed smoked haddock fillets{680%g}(pinboned) and @fresh bay leaves{2} in a shallow pan with enough water to cover. Bring to the boil, cover and simmer for about ~fish{5%minutes}, until cooked through. Remove from pan and leave to cool. Remove the skin from fish, flake into chunks and set aside.

Cook the @rice{170%g} in salted water for about ~rice{10%minutes} and drain. Refresh in cold water, drain again, and leave in the fridge until needed.

Melt the @butterghee{110%g} in a pan over a low heat. Add the @fresh ginger{thumb-sized}(peeled and grated), @spring onions{1%bunch}(or 1 onion) and @garlic{1%clove}. Soften for about ~{5%minutes}, then add the @curry powder{2%tbsp} and @mustard seeds{1%tbsp}. Cook for a further ~{2%minutes}, then add the @tomatoes{2}(de-seeded and chopped) and @lemon juice{4%tbsp}.

Quarter the eggs. Add the fish and rice to the pan and gently heat through. Add the eggs, most of the @fresh coriander{2%handfuls}(chopped) and the @red chilli{1}(finely chopped) and stir gently. Place in a warm serving dish.

Mix the rest of the coriander into the @natural yoghurt{small pot} and serve with the kedgeree.